From: ZeroCD DVD support series
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] usb: gadget: f_mass_storage: fix READ TOC for DVD and Mac OS X

Two problems with the current READ TOC implementation:

1. check_command() mask doesn't include cmnd[2] (Format Field), so
hosts that set the format byte get INVALID FIELD IN CDB. Fix the
mask to allow cmnd[2]: (3<<1) -> (1<<2) | (1<<1).

2. The validation condition rejects valid CDBs that have bits set
in cmnd[1] other than MSF (the SFF8020i legacy format puts format
bits in cmnd[9]). Simplify to only check start_track > 1, since
the format field decoding already handles both modern and legacy
formats.

The kernel already contains SFF8020i decoding (cmnd[9] bits 7:6)
and format 0/1/2 handling from a previous upstream fix. This patch
only corrects the remaining validation and mask issues.

References:
- https://lore.kernel.org/all/20220110062359.5314-2-quic_jackp@quicinc.com/
- MMC-6 spec section 6.25 (READ TOC/PMA/ATIP)

Signed-off-by: ZeroCD patch series
---
 drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_mass_storage.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_mass_storage.c b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_mass_storage.c
index 08e0d1c51..26287b704 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_mass_storage.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_mass_storage.c
@@ -1211,8 +1211,7 @@ static int do_read_toc(struct fsg_common *common, struct fsg_buffhd *bh)
 
 	format = common->cmnd[2] & 0xf;
 
-	if ((common->cmnd[1] & ~0x02) != 0 ||	/* Mask away MSF */
-			(start_track > 1 && format != 0x1)) {
+	if (start_track > 1) {
 		curlun->sense_data = SS_INVALID_FIELD_IN_CDB;
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
@@ -2009,7 +2008,7 @@ static int do_scsi_command(struct fsg_common *common)
 		common->data_size_from_cmnd =
 			get_unaligned_be16(&common->cmnd[7]);
 		reply = check_command(common, 10, DATA_DIR_TO_HOST,
-				      (0xf<<6) | (3<<1), 1,
+				      (0xf<<6) | (1<<2) | (1<<1), 1,
 				      "READ TOC");
 		if (reply == 0)
 			reply = do_read_toc(common, bh);
